  "overview": {
    "title": "Sea and mountain in one park",
    "p1": "Al Hoceima National Park protects a stretch of Mediterranean cliff coast and nearshore waters west of town. Limestone headlands, hidden coves and marine life are the core of the landscape.",
    "p2": "Come for viewpoints, short coastal walks and a sense of how steeply the Rif meets the sea. Cala Iris and Torres de Alcalá sit in or beside this protected shoreline.",
    "p3": "Wear steady shoes, carry water and respect any marked paths or access rules — this is a conservation area, not a city beach."
  },
